\section{Updating named calls}{

The pre-release cleanup completes the argument rename. Use the current
spelling in named calls and in argument lists forwarded to these functions.
The complete function-by-function mapping is shipped as
\code{extdata/argument-renames.csv}.\tabular{ll}{
   Previous argument \tab Current argument \cr
   \code{SM.assay}, \code{SM_assay} \tab \code{smAssay} \cr
   \code{ST.assay}, \code{ST_assay} \tab \code{stAssay} \cr
   \code{min_score} \tab \code{minScore} \cr
   \code{raw.mz.column} \tab \code{rawMzColumn} \cr
   \code{database_local_dir} \tab \code{databaseLocalDir} \cr
   \code{normalisation.type} \tab \code{normalizationType} \cr
   \code{DE.list} \tab \code{deList} \cr
   \code{logFC_threshold} \tab \code{foldChangeThreshold} \cr
}


The migration changes function arguments. Resource columns, saved result
fields and documented workflow configuration fields keep their schemas.
For example, annotation output still includes \code{observed_mz}, and the
workflow's \code{structure} list still uses \code{stability_blocks}.
}

\section{Fold-change units}{

\code{findAllDEMs()} and \code{runDE()} accept \code{foldChangeThreshold} as a ratio of
at least 1: 1.2 represents a 20 percent change and 2 represents a twofold
change. \code{demsHeatmap()} accepts \code{logFCThreshold} on the scale of its \code{logFC}
results. For log2 results, a threshold of 1 selects twofold changes.
}

